rder is causal, not cosmetic. The trailing Critical alert demonstrates the documented alert-lag semantics live. Boot journal on the same session: boot marker at seq 1, newgame marker, **8 deduped warnings** (the baseline set minus SteamAPI.Init, which fires before any mod ctor exists — JOURNAL.md documents that boundary; LogRelay's backfill owns it), 0 red errors, 0 mapgen noise (deaths/downeds gated on ProgramState.Playing after the first boot showed ruins-corpse setup leaking in).\n\n`journal` verb filters verified: `{since_seq:14, limit:5}` -\u003e seq 15-19 with truncated:true; `{types:[letter]}` -\u003e exactly the 3 letters.\n\n**2. Journal survives save/load round-trip without duplication or gap.**\n\n`journal-selftest {steps:[save], save_name:autostart}` (the SaveGame postfix journaled the save), force-kill, relaunch with no -quicktest -\u003e devMode autostart auto-load (the 0.1 fixture hook, working as documented). New session file 20260830T202611:\n\n```\nseq 1        session boot marker\nseq 2-10     9 deduped warnings (baseline 8 + \"hidden ritual precept ... Funeral (no corpse)\",\n             an Ideology backfill that only load-of-save boots produce — benign)\nseq 11       session {kind:loaded} at tick 3647 — game-time continuity across the boundary\nseq 12-17    the alert layer re-noticing the save's state (Critical rescue alert, etc.)\n```\n\nZero duplicated events — 0 letters and 0 selftest strings in the new file; the old session file closed intact at seq 34; both files gap-free (contiguous seq from 1). Red errors this boot: 0.\n\n**3. Overhead measured negligible via AnalyzerBridge/DPA on a running colony.**\n\nDriven through AnalyzerBridge's own file protocol (custom Update profiling):\n\n```\n{\"id\":\"ov1\",\"op\":\"start\",\"category\":\"Update\",\n \"methods\":[\"AutoRimmer.AgentGameComponent:GameComponentUpdate\"],\"durationSeconds\":12}\n-\u003e  averageMs 0.0039, maxMs 0.1068, calls 720, percent 0.0011, at 60.1 tps\n```\n\nThe entire per